SUMMARY:IGC Seminar: How the BAF (SWI/SNF) chromatin remodeling complexes regulate the nucleosomal and subnucleosomal organization of cis regulatory elements in mammalian cells
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Matthieu Gérard (CNRS, I2BC). Title: How the BAF (SWI/SNF) chromatin remodeling complexes regulate the nucleosomal and subnucleosomal organization of cis regulatory elements in mammalian cells.\nHost: Nick Gilbert.\nMatthieu Gérard leads the Mammalian Epigenomics group at I2BC. Research focuses on ATP-dependent chromatin remodelling complexes regulating genome accessibility, enhancer activity, and cell identity.\nOnline via Teams: https://teams.microsoft.com/meet/31448993431281?p=zWVmgVqf3x1VpPgLxn Meeting ID: 314 489 934 312 81 Passcode: Xf7Fw6ds
LOCATION:IGC Lecture Theatre (online via Teams)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
